  ],
  "notes": "Official cause_code/category were TBD in FORM-366 FIELDS block; no block_13 rows were provided, so cause node marked provisional. Bus E-3 loss caused parallel automatic actuations (PCIS Group 2/3/6/10 isolations on Unit 2, PCIS Group 6 on Unit 1 via Main Stack High Radiation logic loss, Reactor Building Ventilation/Secondary Containment isolation, SGTS and Control Room Emergency Ventilation start signals) — these are consequences of the single bus-loss event, not separate causal chains, so only one aggregated Consequence node was created to avoid over-fragmentation; EDG 3 did not start only because it was under maintenance clearance, which is a boundary condition not a separate failure mode. Two previous similar events are referenced by Event Notification number (54144, 54675) rather than formal LER numbers — used as-stated per rule 9, since no LER number was given in the narrative."
